<h2>Changing Litter Types Without Starting a Boycott</h2>
<p>Cats can reject an abrupt litter switch outright, so transition gradually over 1–2 weeks: start with roughly 75% old litter and 25% new, mixed in the same box, and shift the ratio every few days until the new litter is the only one left. If you’re switching because of a suspected preference issue rather than convenience, it’s worth doing the opposite experiment first — offer the new litter in a second box <em>alongside</em> the old one, unmixed, and watch which one actually gets used before committing the whole household to the change.</p>
